          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-17000 target: check sec context RPCs were negotiated",
        "message": "LU-17000 target: check sec context RPCs were negotiated\n\ntgt_handle_request0() sends the reply for SEC_CTX_INIT,\nSEC_CTX_INIT_CONT and SEC_CTX_FINI without calling a handler, relying\non the sptlrpc policy to have prepared it (or set rq_no_reply for ctx\nfini) while unwrapping the request.  Only a policy that negotiates\ncontexts does that and sets rq_ctx_init or rq_ctx_fini, so a request\nwith one of these opcodes that was not handled as context negotiation\nreaches ptlrpc_send_reply() with no reply state.\n\nCheck rq_ctx_init/rq_ctx_fini before taking the shortcut and reject\nany other such request with -EPROTO.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial kerberos=true testlist=sanity-krb5\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-sec env=SHARED_KEY=true\nFixes: 6a0d6dd10e3d (\"LU-6356 tgt: handle sec context requests properly\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Ib1067269a770c81fb860003cfa44cf93a3a770ff\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70260\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Sebastien Buisson <sbuisson@ddn.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
